  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Protection, Assistance and Solutions for Forcibly Displaced Populations in Sub-Saharan Africa</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This action aims to contribute to alleviating protracted forced displacement in Sub-Saharan Africa by:1.To improve the access of forcibly displaced populations, in particular women, persons with disabilities and children, and host/resident communities to effective basic services, accessible housing and economic inclusion2.To enhance the provision of urban and rural green and climate resilient durable solutions (voluntary return, local integration, resettlement) by host/resident communities and countries to forcibly displaced populations, in particular women, persons with disabilities and children3.To promote national and regional policy dialogue and commitments in favour of displaced population, in particular women, persons with disabilities and children, by strengthening policy, legal and regulatory frameworks and via the IGAD Support PlatformThis action tackle the following forced displacement situations: i) Sudanese crisis: Chad and South Sudan; ii) Central Sahel: Burkina Faso, Mali and Niger; iii) protracted situations: IGAD Support Platform, Sudan and South Sudan Solutions Initiative, CAR refugees in Cameroon and CAR refugee returnees, and refugees in Uganda; iv) Emergency Transit Mechanism (ETM) in Rwanda; and v) IDPs in Somalia.</narrative>
  </description>
